    "result_text": "All tests green (11 passed, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes owners return a `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` property (readOnly string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` includes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto(Owner)` that computes the value directly from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n           expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nSince the create response and the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response both flow through `toOwnerDto`, the field is derived consistently from the persisted `firstName`/`lastName` \u2014 matching the test's expectation of `\"LastName, John\"` after creation.\n\nThe new `Cp05Tests` passes and the full suite is green (11/11).",
